<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georgians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Georgians are a Kartvelian-speaking people of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> who form the majority of the population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. Christian since the conversion of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> in the 4th century, they have their own script and church, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgian-orthodox-church">Georgian Orthodox Church</a>. Divided for much of their history among rival kingdoms and principalities, they were united under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagrationi dynasty</a>, most gloriously in the 12th and early 13th centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georgians.jpg" alt="Georgians" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Wagner · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgia,_Kutaisi,_Gelati_Monastery_(29812678274).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
